<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Opioid use disorder, in sustained remission (F11.21)</content>. Sustained remission continues. PHQ-9 2, with no thoughts of suicide. The plan for any future pain is complete: non-opioid treatment first; if an opioid is ever needed after surgery or an injury, the smallest supply for the shortest time from one prescriber, with a support person told, naloxone at hand, and a follow-up visit within a week. [S]<list><item>Keep the pain plan on his phone and share it with any surgeon or emergency team.</item><item>Continue the recovery check at each visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Blindness of both eyes since childhood (H54.0X55)</content>. Eyes comfortable and quiet. [S]<list><item>Yearly ophthalmology review in the spring.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Eye comfort and ocular surface check: pain, redness, discharge</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No pain, redness, or discharge</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Tonometry (eye pressure)</td><td>Every glaucoma visit; for blind eyes, only if pain or redness</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Painless blind eyes, as advised by ophthalmology</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Comprehensive eye examination</td><td>Yearly for blind eyes, or with symptoms</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Ophthalmology examination five months ago; next in the spring</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-9)</td><td>At intake, at six months, and yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 2, read aloud, with item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review and safety plan, with the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline still saved in his phone</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Recovery check: any return to use, cravings, triggers, and supports</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No return to use and no cravings</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Naloxone at home and when traveling</td><td>At intake; check expiry at each visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Both sprays in date</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Drug-use screen (DAST-10)</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>DAST-10 0 six months ago; next at the annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Alcohol screen (AUDIT-C)</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>AUDIT-C 2 six months ago; next at the annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hepatitis C, hepatitis B, and HIV testing</td><td>At entry to care for a person with a substance use disorder</td><td>Due</td><td>At the annual wellness visit next month</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Written plan for any future acute pain or surgery</td><td>Before any planned procedure, and once in remission</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Finished today and saved in an accessible format on his phone</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Accessible documents and communication</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Pain plan and visit summary sent as accessible documents</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medicine labeling in braille or audio</td><td>With every new prescription</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No new prescriptions</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>CDC STEADI fall-risk screen</td><td>Every visit from age 65</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls in six months</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning</td><td>Yearly from age 65</td><td>Due</td><td>At the annual wellness visit next month</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccinations</td><td>Yearly, per the CDC schedule</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza and pneumococcal vaccines at the annual wellness visit next month</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Visit summaries, results, and medicine information delivered in an accessible electronic format, and medicine labels in braille or audio, by the four-week visit. Outcome by 2026-03-31: Visit summaries sent as accessible documents; the pharmacy provides audio labels and a braille label on the naloxone [S]</item><item>Naloxone at home and in his travel bag, with a tactile label, and the people he travels with shown how to use it, by the three-month visit. Outcome by 2026-06-02: Naloxone in both places; travel staff shown how to use it [S]</item><item>Stay in sustained remission, with no return to opioid use, through six months. Outcome by 2026-09-01: No opioid use; DAST-10 0 at intake and no use reported at each visit [S]</item><item>No falls through six months. Outcome by 2026-09-01: No falls [S]</item><item>A written plan for any future acute pain or surgery that uses non-opioid treatment first and builds in safeguards if an opioid is ever needed, by the six-month visit. Outcome by 2026-09-01: Plan written with him and saved in an accessible format [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); The ASAM National Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Opioid Use Disorder: 2020 Focused Update (2020); Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma Preferred Practice Pattern (2025); Vision Rehabilitation Preferred Practice Pattern (2023); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, glaucoma and depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Annual wellness visit in five weeks, with the hepatitis and HIV tests, vaccines, and advance care planning. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-06: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

